<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id3b3f30fac2ac3d812f7387bdff70c3333667e00" commit="684c0a05157b1e5cb4efed3930e11292b6ce5df4" commit_message="Add bounds checking to handle_romentries()  This adds some sanity checks to print a useful error message instead of segfaulting in case the user provides a layout file with obviously incorrect ranges.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=attempted using layout file with invalid boundaries and start &gt; end  Change-Id: Id3b3f30fac2ac3d812f7387bdff70c3333667e00 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320165 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320165" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/65/320165/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I26f26b9643bfc0f6c40a0ae332ea975c582bfe8f" commit="bbae115d303946d63dafde7f2a21b78d0cda78ad" commit_message="Split logic to determine required_erase_size into its own function  This just splits code out of handle_partial_read() to make the caller (handle_partial_read) a bit cleaner and allow us to use the same logic in an upcoming patch.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=tested w/ follow-up patch  Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I26f26b9643bfc0f6c40a0ae332ea975c582bfe8f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320205 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320205" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/05/320205/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9c38ef61d7ced192c0303422756741ab37b4f5de" commit="a75e567c90715a712b34f9a26c849a9e85dff59b" commit_message="Fix math bug in handle_partial_verify()  If required_erase_size does not get set (remains 0), the modulo operation blows up (floating point exception).  The bug is tickled when both --diff and --fast-verify are used since we didn't set required_erase_size in that particular case. --diff makes flashrom read from a file (which doesn't touch the chip and thus skips alignment logic) and then &quot;--fast-verify&quot; causes handle_partial_verify() to be called.  To avoid this problem, this patch makes it so that we set required_erase_size whenever a partial read/verify takes place.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=used servo to write content to a region while employing &quot;--diff&quot; and &quot;--fast-verify&quot;  Change-Id: I9c38ef61d7ced192c0303422756741ab37b4f5de Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320206 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320206" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/06/320206/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I1f620d206458cda3e66300be3fc052e2780d9b1b" commit="030b9ec8f3aa65b2723cbc1fc38101f1b29ba88e" commit_message="FROMLIST: clk: add flag for clocks that need to be enabled on rate changes  Some clocks need to be enabled to accept rate changes. This patch adds a new flag CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE that lets clk_change_rate enable the clock before trying to change the rate and disable it again afterwards. This of course doesn't effect clocks that are already running at that point, as their refcount will only temporarily increase.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48588, chrome-os-partner:34330 TEST=Minnie BT works w/ USB webcam plugged in.  Change-Id: I1f620d206458cda3e66300be3fc052e2780d9b1b Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; Tested-by: Sjoerd Simons &lt;sjoerd.simons@collabora.co.uk&gt; Reviewed-by: Sjoerd Simons &lt;sjoerd.simons@collabora.co.uk&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7907161/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320540 Tested-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320540" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/40/320540/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ia8265a5a41bfa8865f6acc8ebf4bb79b388bd81b" commit="83b05ee7da6366cb4b0dc70c678486d5bbbed498" commit_message="BACKPORT: clk: rockchip: handle mux dependency of fractional dividers  The fractional dividers of Rockchip SoCs contain an &quot;auto-gating-feature&quot; that requires the downstream mux to actually point to the fractional divider and the fractional divider gate to be enabled, for it to really accept changes to the divider ratio.  The downstream muxes themselfs are not generic enough to include them directly into the fractional divider, as they have varying sources of parent clocks including not only clocks related to the fractional dividers but other clocks as well.  To solve this, allow our clock branches to specify direct child clock- branches in the new child property, let the fractional divider register its downstream mux through this and add a clock notifier that temporarily switches the mux setting when it notices rate changes to the fractional divider.  NOTE:   This is a significant backport.  The chromeos-3.14 kernel introduced   commit 039c85487faec (&quot;FROMLIST: clk: Add safe switch hook&quot;) which   moved the clk post-rate-change notifications to a block after _all_   clock rate changes were complete.    This breaks the current special handling for fractional dividers, as   the notifier that remuxes back to the original parent from the   temporal one needs to run after the fractional rate change but before   the mux rate gets handled. So to handle this without a notifier, we   copy the fraction clk_ops, set a new set_rate callback that does this   and calls the original set_rate in between.    The clock-framework itself is supposed to get a completely new   framework for handling all those clock-types depending on other   clock-types (like our armclk and fractional dividers .. also Qualcomm   cpuclk, etc) at some point in the future, so this is not meant for   upstream, as hacking up the fractional clk_ops is pretty ugly and the   original change that introduced the incompatibility also is one of   those cases for the that new framework.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48588, chrome-os-partner:34330 TEST=Minnie BT works w/ USB webcam plugged in.  Change-Id: Ia8265a5a41bfa8865f6acc8ebf4bb79b388bd81b Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; Tested-by: Sjoerd Simons &lt;sjoerd.simons@collabora.co.uk&gt; Reviewed-by: Sjoerd Simons &lt;sjoerd.simons@collabora.co.uk&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7907181/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320542 Tested-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Heiko Stübner &lt;mmind00@googlemail.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="320542" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/42/320542/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I5971ff0f365c6695b2481e3d2d0f4929e4a2e93f" commit="ab3b0b80e091f5581260cc7f57e92468f9a54b06" commit_message="CHROMIUM: clk: rockchip: never use USB PHY clock; SCLK_UART0 use fractional clock  Previously we were using the USB PHY clock as the source for UART0 to get high speed UART.  However, it turns out that some usage of the USB port (like hooking up to a webcam) causes that clock to be unsuitble to use as the UART source clock.  This is probably the same thing that was described in &lt;http://crosreview.com/229554&gt;, but at that time we believed the problem to be a failing of the particular PHY associated with the EHCI port. Now that we're seeing the same problem on the DWC2 ports it seems more like a systemic problem.  Anyway, now that we've fixed the driver for the fractional clock we can use it for the UART.  Hooray.  Upstream has done more with fractional clocks.  Since we're pretty hopelessly different from upstream clock stuff, we'll just glom this change in and change the one fractional clock that we need.  This also pulls in a fix for a section mismatch that was fixed upstream in commit 5b73840375e3 (&quot;clk: rockchip: fix section mismatches with new child-clocks&quot;).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48588, chrome-os-partner:34330 TEST=Minnie BT works w/ USB webcam plugged in.  Change-Id: I5971ff0f365c6695b2481e3d2d0f4929e4a2e93f Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320543 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320543" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/43/320543/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2449c8d79b4a74f4865dd1234fb253bcdac66a31" commit="5a5e064ae46441d63c85e29ac0430dd5ecce14d8" commit_message="vboot_hash: check the current hash is for the right region  With the RO region being added to software sync, up to two hashes will be requested during boot. Currently if vboot_hash has a valid hash when the EC gets an EC_VBOOT_HASH_GET host command then it will return that hash. When the EC gets a request for the RO hash after it has calculated the RW hash it returns the RW hash in the response.  This change will add a check that the EC not only has a valid hash, but that it is for the correct region.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=Try to get the RO and RW hashes from depthcharge and make sure they match the values gotten using ectool  Change-Id: I2449c8d79b4a74f4865dd1234fb253bcdac66a31 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/318861 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="318861" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/61/318861/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3494ed7d207e769fe081b4442fd298b4e481e0a7" commit="2a2f17a05f3bd3a8d0b56232c9242c0833580836" commit_message="Chell: modify led setting for OEM spec  Modify the led blink white at battery capacity less than 12%.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=check the led blink white at battery capacity less than 12%  Change-Id: I3494ed7d207e769fe081b4442fd298b4e481e0a7 Signed-off-by: Bruce.Wan &lt;Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319729 Commit-Ready: Bruce Wan &lt;Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com&gt; Tested-by: Bruce Wan &lt;Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319729" owner_email="Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/29/319729/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I62ac675a34694a537af3dc48d5e53ddc2a3a8c5d" commit="88b49d3d6eac101d75236a248ad45a9a8a8e5b34" commit_message="CHROMIUM: sdhci: quirk for reset on tuning timeout  In some cases, data inhibit bits are not released on tuning timeout and will hang system.  Reset the controller after a tuning timeout to avoid this.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48472 TEST=force tuning timeouts  Change-Id: I62ac675a34694a537af3dc48d5e53ddc2a3a8c5d Signed-off-by: Christopher Freeman &lt;cfreeman@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317923 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317923" owner_email="cfreeman@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/23/317923/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia2a66ebec162ba3ab2de2bc0f7183c8ceb5fce8a" commit="0a96209793966dcabb8ba534aa5af0f243de3478" commit_message="frecon: Free drmVersion after printing it  ... not before  BUG=none TEST=run on daisy  Change-Id: Ia2a66ebec162ba3ab2de2bc0f7183c8ceb5fce8a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320596 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320596" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/96/320596/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I52e0816892acdc9891be08fafdbefa03cbe7691d" commit="d23d3846584a63c0d165132f9cf77e4ebde9a83a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Add generic way to find wakeup_type  This adds a generic way to get the wakeup_type for a system. It works if the firmware doesn't get in the way of the kernel receiving interrupts.  This only works for wakeup_sources that are attached to a device.  Backported from 3.18 patch 04f54fcce2ccc34fea552acc9d6d8cc6788bc3df.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:41007 TEST=on glados: echo automatic &gt; /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/device/power/wakeup_type echo +10 &gt; /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/wakealarm; powerd_dbus_suspend Check that /sys/power/wakeup_type is automatic after the system wakes from suspend  Original-Change-Id: I2ccd2e49cf2bc37d36b342f613562200f299319c Original-signed-off-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Original-reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309001 Original-reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I52e0816892acdc9891be08fafdbefa03cbe7691d Signed-off-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320433 Reviewed-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320433" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/320433/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib9251261b466281d5b8cda74b296d8e4d60acc61" commit="7835c4346ddda4788bdd5756c1d85b53399150da" commit_message="eeprom: Change return type of &quot;size&quot; function to int  This is intended to allow error handling in case the &quot;size&quot; function fails. Up to this point we only worked with hard-coded values so error checking didn't matter. This will make it so that we can leverage external programs (flashrom and possibly others) and handle errors if need be.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=tested on cyan w/ follow-up patch, compiled for ARM and x86 platforms  Change-Id: Ib9251261b466281d5b8cda74b296d8e4d60acc61 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks